{"black_box_warning":{"current_value":"No FDA boxed warning identified in selected current DailyMed label.","fda_source_urls":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%228bf27097-4870-43fb-94f0-f3d0871d1eec%22&limit=5","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/210365s021lbl.pdf"],"proposed_value":"No FDA boxed warning identified in selected current FDA/openFDA label.","rationale":"The no-boxed-warning conclusion is supportable, but the row cites DailyMed for the boxed-warning field. The audit policy requires FDA/openFDA, FDA labels, or Drugs@FDA only for this field.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect"},"blocking_questions":[],"fact_checks":[{"current_value":"cannabidiol","field":"generic_name","proposed_value":"cannabidiol","rationale":"FDA labeling identifies EPIDIOLEX as cannabidiol oral solution.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/210365s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Epidiolex; Epidyolex","field":"trade_names","proposed_value":"Epidiolex; Epidyolex","rationale":"Epidiolex is the FDA-labeled US product; EMA lists Epidyolex with active substance cannabidiol.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/210365s021lbl.pdf","https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/medicines/human/EPAR/epidyolex"]},{"current_value":"","field":"alternate_generic_names","proposed_value":"","rationale":"No separate alternate generic name requiring a separate row was identified; CBD is already captured as a search alias, not a distinct generic drug.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK548890/"]},{"current_value":"CBD","field":"pubmed_search_aliases","proposed_value":"CBD; GWP42003-P","rationale":"CBD is verified. GWP42003-P is a recurring trial/intervention name in ClinicalTrials.gov records for cannabidiol and should be searchable to prevent missed RCTs.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"missing","supporting_sources":["https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT02091375","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT02224560","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT02224690","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT02544763"]},{"current_value":"Yes","field":"available_in_us","proposed_value":"Yes","rationale":"EPIDIOLEX is FDA-approved and marketed under NDA 210365.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/210365s021lbl.pdf","https://www.fda.gov/news-events/public-health-focus/fda-regulation-cannabis-and-cannabis-derived-products-including-cannabidiol-cbd"]},{"current_value":"2018","field":"year_fda_cleared","proposed_value":"2018","rationale":"FDA labeling states Initial U.S. Approval: 2018. The deterministic update-check concern is a source-concordance false positive, not a factual contradiction.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/210365s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"LGS; Dravet; TSC","field":"epilepsy_type","proposed_value":"LGS; Dravet; TSC","rationale":"FDA labeling indicates seizures associated with Lennox-Gastaut syndrome, Dravet syndrome, or tuberous sclerosis complex.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/210365s021lbl.pdf","https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/medicines/human/EPAR/epidyolex"]},{"current_value":"Oral solution","field":"formulations_available","proposed_value":"Oral solution","rationale":"FDA label lists EPIDIOLEX 100 mg/mL oral solution.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/210365s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"5-25 mg/kg/day divided BID depending on syndrome","field":"typical_doses_per_day","proposed_value":"5-25 mg/kg/day divided BID depending on syndrome","rationale":"FDA label supports 5 mg/kg/day starting dose, 10-20 mg/kg/day for LGS/Dravet, and 25 mg/kg/day maintenance for TSC, administered twice daily.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/210365s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"10 mg/kg/day for LGS/Dravet; 25 mg/kg/day for TSC target regimen","field":"minimum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"10 mg/kg/day for LGS/Dravet; 25 mg/kg/day for TSC target regimen","rationale":"FDA dosing supports 10 mg/kg/day as the maintenance dosage for LGS/Dravet and 25 mg/kg/day as the recommended TSC maintenance dosage; RCT evidence also supports 10 mg/kg/day cannabidiol in LGS/Dravet.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/210365s021lbl.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29768152/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32119035/"]},{"current_value":"25 mg/kg/day for TSC; 20 mg/kg/day for Dravet/LGS","field":"maximum_approved_daily_dose","proposed_value":"25 mg/kg/day for TSC; 20 mg/kg/day for Dravet/LGS","rationale":"FDA dosing sections support these syndrome-specific maximum or recommended maintenance regimens.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/210365s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Liver","field":"major_organ_for_metabolism","proposed_value":"Liver","rationale":"FDA clinical pharmacology states cannabidiol is metabolized in the liver and gut, primarily in the liver.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/210365s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Effective ~17 h; terminal ~56-61 h","field":"half_life_range","proposed_value":"Terminal plasma half-life 56-61 h after twice-daily dosing for 7 days","rationale":"FDA labeling supports terminal plasma half-life of 56-61 h. I did not find a trusted row-cited source supporting the effective half-life value of ~17 h.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"missing_source","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/210365s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Inhibits CYP2C19 and can inhibit CYP2C9/UGT pathways; affected by CYP3A4/CYP2C19 modulators","field":"enzyme_inducing_or_inhibiting","proposed_value":"Substrate of CYP3A4/CYP2C19; inhibits CYP2C19 and may inhibit CYP2C9, UGT1A9, and UGT2B7; strong CYP3A4/CYP2C19 inducers reduce exposure","rationale":"The current value is broadly consistent but should be made more precise: FDA labeling identifies CYP3A4/CYP2C19 metabolism and substrate status, inhibition potential, UGT inhibition, and decreased exposure with strong CYP3A4/CYP2C19 induction.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/210365s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"CNS: somnolence 23-32%, GI: decreased appetite 16-22%, GI: diarrhea 9-20%, hepatic: transaminase elevation 8-13%, constitutional: fatigue/malaise 11%","field":"adverse_symptoms_percentages","proposed_value":"CNS: somnolence 13-25%, GI: decreased appetite 16-22%, GI: diarrhea 9-31%, hepatic: transaminases elevated 8-25%, constitutional: fatigue/malaise/asthenia 5-12%","rationale":"FDA adverse-reaction tables for LGS/Dravet and TSC support the proposed ranges. The current row misses the TSC diarrhea and transaminase maxima and includes a somnolence maximum not supported by the selected FDA label tables.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/210365s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Precise human anticonvulsant mechanisms are unknown; effects do not appear to be mediated by CB1/CB2 cannabinoid receptors, with GPR55, TRPV1, and adenosine-mediated signaling proposed.","field":"mechanism_of_action","proposed_value":"Precise human anticonvulsant mechanisms are unknown; cannabidiol does not appear to exert its anticonvulsant effects through interaction with cannabinoid receptors.","rationale":"FDA labeling supports the unknown mechanism and lack of apparent cannabinoid-receptor mediation. A trusted row-cited source was not found for the GPR55, TRPV1, and adenosine-mediated signaling claims.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"missing_source","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/210365s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Limited","field":"mechanism_confidence","proposed_value":"Limited","rationale":"Consistent with FDA labeling that the precise human anticonvulsant mechanism is unknown.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/210365s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"No clinically meaningful QT prolongation established","field":"qt_interval_effect","proposed_value":"Concentration-dependent QTc prolongation observed; at recommended monotherapy exposures with a high-fat meal, EPIDIOLEX did not prolong QTc by more than 10 ms; QTc effect at increased exposures from food, concomitant medications, or alcohol is unknown","rationale":"FDA labeling is more nuanced than the current text: it reports concentration-dependent QTc prolongation but no >10 ms QTc prolongation at recommended monotherapy exposures with a high-fat meal.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/210365s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"NCBI LiverTox anticonvulsants table; Epilepsy Society ASM list; FDA/DailyMed labeling; American Epilepsy Society 2024 U.S. ASM summary","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA or FDA-approved labeling for Epidiolex; NCBI LiverTox cannabidiol monograph; EMA Epidyolex EPAR; PubMed/ClinicalTrials.gov RCT records listed in pubmed_phase_ii_iii_rct_links","rationale":"The current source list includes DailyMed and sources outside the trusted-domain list. FDA/openFDA/FDA label, NCBI, EMA, PubMed, and ClinicalTrials.gov sources support the retained row facts more directly.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/210365s021lbl.pdf","https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%228bf27097-4870-43fb-94f0-f3d0871d1eec%22&limit=5","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK548890/","https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/medicines/human/EPAR/epidyolex"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed labeling; American Epilepsy Society 2024 U.S. ASM summary","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA-approved labeling for Epidiolex, section 12.1 Clinical Pharmacology / Mechanism of Action","rationale":"The current source string includes DailyMed and AES; the FDA label directly supports only the narrower mechanism statement.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/210365s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA/AES summary","field":"mechanism_source_tier","proposed_value":"FDA labeling","rationale":"The retained mechanism should be sourced to FDA labeling only unless a trusted peer-reviewed source is added for the extra mechanistic hypotheses.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/210365s021lbl.pdf"]}],"generic_name":"cannabidiol","missing_rcts":[{"pmid":"33797076","proposed_link_text":"Privitera2021|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33797076/","title":"Time to onset of cannabidiol (CBD) treatment effect in Lennox-Gastaut syndrome: Analysis from two randomized controlled trials.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33797076/","why_relevant":"PubMe