dian-percent-change differentials: Thiele2021 30.1%, Miller2020 25.7%, Devinsky2018b 41.9-17.2=24.7, Thiele2018 43.9-21.8=22.1, Devinsky2017 adjusted median difference 22.8 percentage points.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33346789/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32119035/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29768152/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29395273/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28538134/"]},{"current_value":"Thiele2021|30.1|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33346789/|224; Miller2020|25.7|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32119035/|198; Thiele2018|22.1|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29395273/|171; Devinsky2018b|24.7|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29768152/|225; Devinsky2017|22.8|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28538134/|120","field":"plot_diff_median_pct_change_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"Thiele2021|30.1|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33346789/|224; Miller2020|25.7|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32119035/|198; Thiele2018|22.1|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29395273/|171; Devinsky2018b|24.7|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29768152/|225; Devinsky2017|22.8|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28538134/|120","rationale":"Plot entries match the cited maximum approved/effective regimen outcome values and sample sizes used in the row bundle.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33346789/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32119035/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29395273/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29768152/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28538134/"]},{"current_value":"5 % (drug minus placebo seizure-freedom differential at maximum effective dose/regimen: Devinsky2017 CBD 20 mg/kg/day 5%)","field":"diff_seizure_freedom_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"5 % (drug minus placebo seizure-freedom differential at maximum effective dose/regimen: Devinsky2017 CBD 20 mg/kg/day 5%)","rationale":"Devinsky2017 reports 5% seizure-free with cannabidiol versus 0% with placebo; differential is 5 percentage points.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28538134/"]},{"current_value":"Devinsky2017|5|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28538134/|120","field":"plot_diff_seizure_freedom_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"Devinsky2017|5|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28538134/|120","rationale":"Plot label, value, URL, and N match the seizure-freedom result cited from Devinsky2017.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28538134/"]}],"overall_status":"needs_update","proposed_row_updates":[{"current_value":"CNS: somnolence 23-32%, GI: decreased appetite 16-22%, GI: diarrhea 9-20%, hepatic: transaminase elevation 8-13%, constitutional: fatigue/malaise 11%","field":"adverse_symptoms_percentages","proposed_value":"CNS: somnolence 13-25%, GI: decreased appetite 16-22%, GI: diarrhea 9-31%, hepatic: transaminases elevated 8-25%, constitutional: fatigue/malaise/asthenia 5-12%","reason":"Align adverse-event ranges with FDA label Tables 3 and 4 across LGS/Dravet and TSC.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/210365s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed SPL; status=no_boxed_warning_in_selected_label; setid=8bf27097-4870-43fb-94f0-f3d0871d1eec; published=Nov 17, 2025; title=EPIDIOLEX (CANNABIDIOL) SOLUTION [JAZZ PHARMACEUTICALS, INC.]; url=https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=8bf27097-4870-43fb-94f0-f3d0871d1eec","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA drug label API; status=no_boxed_warning_in_selected_fda_label; spl_set_id=8bf27097-4870-43fb-94f0-f3d0871d1eec; effective_time=20250731; title=Epidiolex / CANNABIDIOL; api_url=https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%228bf27097-4870-43fb-94f0-f3d0871d1eec%22&limit=5","reason":"DailyMed is not permitted for FDA boxed-warning verification; use FDA/openFDA metadata.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%228bf27097-4870-43fb-94f0-f3d0871d1eec%22&limit=5","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/210365s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"No FDA boxed warning identified in selected current DailyMed label.","field":"fda_black_box_warning","proposed_value":"No FDA boxed warning identified in selected current FDA/openFDA label.","reason":"Same conclusion, corrected source language.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%228bf27097-4870-43fb-94f0-f3d0871d1eec%22&limit=5"]},{"current_value":"Effective ~17 h; terminal ~56-61 h","field":"half_life_range","proposed_value":"Terminal plasma half-life 56-61 h after twice-daily dosing for 7 days","reason":"FDA label supports terminal half-life only; no trusted source was found for the effective half-life value.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/210365s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Precise human anticonvulsant mechanisms are unknown; effects do not appear to be mediated by CB1/CB2 cannabinoid receptors, with GPR55, TRPV1, and adenosine-mediated signaling proposed.","field":"mechanism_of_action","proposed_value":"Precise human anticonvulsant mechanisms are unknown; cannabidiol does not appear to exert its anticonvulsant effects through interaction with cannabinoid receptors.","reason":"FDA labeling supports the narrower statement; the additional mechanistic hypotheses lack a trusted row-cited source.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/210365s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed labeling; American Epilepsy Society 2024 U.S. ASM summary","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA-approved labeling for Epidiolex, section 12.1 Clinical Pharmacology / Mechanism of Action","reason":"Mechanism statement should cite a trusted source that directly supports it.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/210365s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA/AES summary","field":"mechanism_source_tier","proposed_value":"FDA labeling","reason":"AES summary was not verified from the trusted-domain list and is not needed for the FDA-supported mechanism statement.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/210365s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"No clinically meaningful QT prolongation established","field":"qt_interval_effect","proposed_value":"Concentration-dependent QTc prolongation observed; at recommended monotherapy exposures with a high-fat meal, EPIDIOLEX did not prolong QTc by more than 10 ms; QTc effect at increased exposures from food, concomitant medications, or alcohol is unknown","reason":"FDA label supports a more nuanced QT statement.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/210365s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Inhibits CYP2C19 and can inhibit CYP2C9/UGT pathways; affected by CYP3A4/CYP2C19 modulators","field":"enzyme_inducing_or_inhibiting","proposed_value":"Substrate of CYP3A4/CYP2C19; inhibits CYP2C19 and may inhibit CYP2C9, UGT1A9, and UGT2B7; strong CYP3A4/CYP2C19 inducers reduce exposure","reason":"More closely matches FDA drug-interaction and pharmacokinetic wording.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/210365s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"CBD","field":"pubmed_search_aliases","proposed_value":"CBD; GWP42003-P","reason":"GWP42003-P is an important trial code/intervention name for cannabidiol in ClinicalTrials.gov records.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT02091375","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT02224560","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT02224690","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT02544763"]},{"current_value":"NCBI LiverTox anticonvulsants table; Epilepsy Society ASM list; FDA/DailyMed labeling; American Epilepsy Society 2024 U.S. ASM summary","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA or FDA-approved labeling for Epidiolex; NCBI LiverTox cannabidiol monograph; EMA Epidyolex EPAR; PubMed/ClinicalTrials.gov RCT records listed in pubmed_phase_ii_iii_rct_links","reason":"Replace non-trusted or non-specific row sources with trusted sources that directly support the populated facts.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/210365s021lbl.pdf","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK548890/","https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/medicines/human/EPAR/epidyolex"]},{"current_value":"OBrien2022|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35802375/; Thiele2021|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33346789/; Miller2020|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32119035/; Thiele2018|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29395273/; Devinsky2018b|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29768152/; Devinsky2018|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29540584/; Devinsky2017|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28538134/","field":"pubmed_phase_ii_iii_rct_links","proposed_value":"OBrien2022|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35802375/; Thiele2021|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33346789/; Miller2020|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32119035/; Thiele2018|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29395273/; Devinsky2018b|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29768152/; Devinsky2018|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29540584/; Devinsky2017|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28538134/; Privitera2021|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33797076/","reason":"Privitera2021 is a post hoc analysis of two randomized placebo-controlled phase 3 LGS cannabidiol trials; append only if secondary RCT analyses are within CSV scope.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33797076/"]}],"rct_link_checks":[{"label":"OBrien2022","pmid":"35802375","proposed_action":"Retain pending row-policy review; do not use for RR50/MPC/seizure-freedom rollups.","rationale":"Correct drug and placebo-controlled randomized transdermal cannabidiol focal-epilepsy trial, but PubMed did not clearly verify phase II/III classification, and no significant double-blind efficacy difference was reported.","status":"insufficient_evidence","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35802375/"},{"label":"Thiele2021","pmid":"33346789","proposed_action":"Keep.","rationale":"Correct cannabidiol assignment; double-blind placebo-controlled randomized trial in TSC; ClinicalTrials.gov NCT02544763 is phase 3; outcome value 30.1% is supported.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33346789/"},{"label":"Miller2020","pmid":"32119035","proposed_action":"Keep; resolve deterministic concordance warning as false positive.","rationale":"Correct drug and intervention: cannabidiol oral solution 10 or 20 mg/kg/day versus matched placebo in Dravet syndrome. It is a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled GWPCARE2 trial; ClinicalTrials.gov NCT02224703 is phase 3.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32119035/"},{"label":"Thiele2018","pmid":"29395273","proposed_action":"Keep.","rationale":"Correct cannabidiol assignment; randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled phase 3 GWPCARE4 trial in LGS; outcome value 22.1 percentage points is supported.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29395273/"},{"label":"Devinsky2018b","pmid":"29768152","proposed_action":"Keep.","rationale":"Correct cannabidiol assignment; randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled phase 3 GWPCARE3 trial in LGS; outcome value 24.7 percentage points is supported.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29768152/"},{"label":"Devinsky2018","pmid":"29540584","proposed_action":"Keep; do not use for maximum-dose efficacy rollup.","rationale":"Correct drug; randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled phase 2 dose-ranging safety/PK trial in Dravet syndrome. It does not provide extractable maximum-dose efficacy outcomes for the row rollups.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29540584/"},{"label":"Devinsky2017","pmid":"28538134","proposed_action":"Keep.","rationale":"Correct cannabidiol assignment; randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled Dravet trial; outcome values for MPC, RR50, and seizure freedom are supported.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28538134/"}],"source_updates":[{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed SPL; status=no_boxed_warning_in_selected_label; setid=8bf27097-4870-43fb-94f0-f3d0871d1eec; published=Nov 17, 2025; title=EPIDIOLEX (CANNABIDIOL) SOLUTION [JAZZ PHARMACEUTICALS, INC.]; url=https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=8bf27097-4870-43fb-94f0-f3d0871d1eec","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA drug label API; status=no_boxed_warning_in_selected_fda_label; spl_set_id=8bf27097-4870-43fb-94f0-f3d0871d1eec; effective_time=20250731; title=Epidiolex / CANNABIDIOL; api_url=https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%228bf27097-4870-43fb-94f0-f3d0871d1eec%22&limit=5","reason":"Black-box warning verification must use FDA/openFDA, FDA labels, or Drugs@FDA, not DailyMed.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%228bf27097-4870-43fb-94f0-f3d0871d1eec%22&limit=5"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed labeling; American Epilepsy Society 2024 U.S. ASM summary","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA-approved labeling for Epidiolex, section 12.1 Clinical Pharmacology / Mechanism of Action","reason":"Current source does not support all mechanism text and includes non-preferred/non-trusted source naming.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/210365s021lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"NCBI LiverTox anticonvulsants table; Epilepsy Society ASM list; FDA/DailyMed labeling; American Epilepsy Society 2024 U.S. ASM summary","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA or FDA-approved labeling for Epidiolex; NCBI LiverTox cannabidiol monograph; EMA Epidyolex EPAR; PubMed/ClinicalTrials.gov RCT records listed in pubmed_phase_ii_iii_rct_links","reason":"Use trusted domains and sources that directly support row facts.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/210365s021lbl.pdf","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK548890/","https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/medicines/human/EPAR/epidyolex","https://clinicaltrials.gov/"]}],"summary":"Cannabidiol is the correct row drug; Epidiolex/Epidyolex aliases are appropriate, and the main FDA indication, dosing, formulation, metabolism, and RCT outcome values are largely verified. Updates are needed for black-box warning source compliance, adverse-event ranges, QT wording, half-life sourcing, mechanism sourcing, evidence source cleanup, PubMed alias expansion, and possible handling of the secondary Privitera2021 RCT analysis."}
